# Phase 3: Code Review Report — Cycle 2

**Reviewed:** 2026-05-07
**Depth:** standard
**Files Reviewed:** 19
**Cycle:** 2 of 3 (--auto fix loop)
**Status:** issues_found

## Summary

All 13 cycle-1 findings (5 BLOCKER + 8 WARNING) are RESOLVED. The fixes match what cycle 1 demanded — the cooldown gate, the redact helper, the typed-error wrapper, the token-capture reordering, the password masking, the unload shutdown call, and the substantive blocking-call test all land correctly. Test coverage on the regressions is solid (each cycle-1 ID has at least one named regression test asserting the corrected behaviour).

However, cycle-1 CR-04 was **scoped too narrowly**. The fix added `set_active_child` and applied it to the 3 sites cycle 1 enumerated (`__init__.py`, `coordinator._recover_from_auth_error`, `config_flow._create_entry`), but a **4th call site exists in `api/fetcher.py:54`** — `client.set_child(child_index_or_identifier)` invoked directly on every poll for `ParentClient`, outside the surrounding try/except. A `pronotepy.exceptions.CryptoError` raised here on a stale parent session bypasses the typed-exception facade entirely, defeats D-09's silent-recovery routing, and surfaces in HA logs with un-redacted pronotepy text. This is a BLOCKER because it nullifies the recovery contract for parent accounts — exactly the path WR-04's cooldown was added to protect.

One WARNING and three INFO items round out the report: the WARNING is a reauth-loop hazard around `_last_recovery_at` not being reset on a successful recovery (cooldown will continue blocking even after the user fixes their password), and the INFO items cover redact-pattern gaps and a fragile mock construction.

